{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "id": "kjv-job-031",
  "collection": "kjv-bible",
  "document_type": "bible_chapter",
  "number": 31,
  "title": "Job 31",
  "display_title": "Job 31",
  "translation": "King James Version",
  "translationCode": "KJV",
  "bookId": "job",
  "book": "Job",
  "bookName": "Job",
  "bookOrder": 18,
  "testament": "old",
  "chapter": 31,
  "sortOrder": 18031,
  "verseCount": 40,
  "aliases": [
    "Job"
  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "verse-001",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 1,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:31:1",
      "numberLabel": "1",
      "text": "I made a covenant with mine eyes; why then should I think upon a maid?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 31:1",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:31:1"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-002",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 2,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:31:2",
      "numberLabel": "2",
      "text": "For what portion of God is there from above? and what inheritance of the Almighty from on high?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 31:2",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:31:2"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-003",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 3,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:31:3",
      "numberLabel": "3",
      "text": "Is not destruction to the wicked? and a strange punishment to the workers of iniquity?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 31:3",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:31:3"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-004",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 4,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:31:4",
      "numberLabel": "4",
      "text": "Doth not he see my ways, and count all my steps?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 31:4",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:31:4"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-005",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 5,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:31:5",
      "numberLabel": "5",
      "text": "If I have walked with vanity, or if my foot hath hasted to deceit;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 31:5",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:31:5"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-006",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 6,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:31:6",
      "numberLabel": "6",
      "text": "Let me be weighed in an even balance that God may know mine integrity.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 31:6",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:31:6"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-007",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 7,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:31:7",
      "numberLabel": "7",
      "text": "If my step hath turned out of the way, and mine heart walked after mine eyes, and if any blot hath cleaved to mine hands;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 31:7",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:31:7"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-008",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 8,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:31:8",
      "numberLabel": "8",
      "text": "Then let me sow, and let another eat; yea, let my offspring be rooted out.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 31:8",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:31:8"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-009",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 9,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:31:9",
      "numberLabel": "9",
      "text": "If mine heart have been deceived by a woman, or if I have laid wait at my neighbour’s door;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 31:9",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:31:9"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-010",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 10,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:31:10",
      "numberLabel": "10",
      "text": "Then let my wife grind unto another, and let others bow down upon her.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 31:10",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:31:10"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-011",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 11,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:31:11",
      "numberLabel": "11",
      "text": "For this is an heinous crime; yea, it is an iniquity to be punished by the judges.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 31:11",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:31:11"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-012",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 12,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:31:12",
      "numberLabel": "12",
      "text": "For it is a fire that consumeth to destruction, and would root out all mine increase.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 31:12",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:31:12"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-013",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 13,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:31:13",
      "numberLabel": "13",
      "text": "If I did despise the cause of my manservant or of my maidservant, when they contended with me;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 31:13",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:31:13"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-014",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 14,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:31:14",
      "numberLabel": "14",
      "text": "What then shall I do when God riseth up? and when he visiteth, what shall I answer him?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 31:14",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:31:14"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-015",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 15,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:31:15",
      "numberLabel": "15",
      "text": "Did not he that made me in the womb make him? and did not one fashion us in the womb?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 31:15",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:31:15"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-016",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 16,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:31:16",
      "numberLabel": "16",
      "text": "If I have withheld the poor from their desire, or have caused the eyes of the widow to fail;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 31:16",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:31:16"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-017",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 17,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:31:17",
      "numberLabel": "17",
      "text": "Or have eaten my morsel myself alone, and the fatherless hath not eaten thereof;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 31:17",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:31:17"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-018",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 18,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:31:18",
      "numberLabel": "18",
      "text": "(For from my youth he was brought up with me, as with a father, and I have guided her from my mother’s womb;)",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 31:18",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:31:18"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-019",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 19,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:31:19",
      "numberLabel": "19",
      "text": "If I have seen any perish for want of clothing, or any poor without covering;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 31:19",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:31:19"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-020",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 20,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:31:20",
      "numberLabel": "20",
      "text": "If his loins have not blessed me, and if he were not warmed with the fleece of my sheep;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 31:20",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:31:20"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-021",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 21,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:31:21",
      "numberLabel": "21",
      "text": "If I have lifted up my hand against the fatherless, when I saw my help in the gate:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 31:21",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:31:21"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-022",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 22,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:31:22",
      "numberLabel": "22",
      "text": "Then let mine arm fall from my shoulder blade, and mine arm be broken from the bone.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 31:22",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:31:22"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-023",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 23,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:31:23",
      "numberLabel": "23",
      "text": "For destruction from God was a terror to me, and by reason of his highness I could not endure.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 31:23",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:31:23"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-024",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 24,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:31:24",
      "numberLabel": "24",
      "text": "If I have made gold my hope, or have said to the fine gold, Thou art my confidence;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 31:24",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:31:24"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-025",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 25,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:31:25",
      "numberLabel": "25",
      "text": "If I rejoiced because my wealth was great, and because mine hand had gotten much;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 31:25",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:31:25"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-026",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 26,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:31:26",
      "numberLabel": "26",
      "text": "If I beheld the sun when it shined, or the moon walking in brightness;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 31:26",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:31:26"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-027",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 27,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:31:27",
      "numberLabel": "27",
      "text": "And my heart hath been secretly enticed, or my mouth hath kissed my hand:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 31:27",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:31:27"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-028",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 28,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:31:28",
      "numberLabel": "28",
      "text": "This also were an iniquity to be punished by the judge: for I should have denied the God that is above.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 31:28",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:31:28"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-029",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 29,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:31:29",
      "numberLabel": "29",
      "text": "If I rejoiced at the destruction of him that hated me, or lifted up myself when evil found him:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 31:29",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:31:29"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-030",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 30,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:31:30",
      "numberLabel": "30",
      "text": "Neither have I suffered my mouth to sin by wishing a curse to his soul.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 31:30",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:31:30"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-031",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 31,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:31:31",
      "numberLabel": "31",
      "text": "If the men of my tabernacle said not, Oh that we had of his flesh! we cannot be satisfied.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 31:31",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:31:31"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-032",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 32,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:31:32",
      "numberLabel": "32",
      "text": "The stranger did not lodge in the street: but I opened my doors to the traveller.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 31:32",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:31:32"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-033",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 33,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:31:33",
      "numberLabel": "33",
      "text": "If I covered my transgressions as Adam, by hiding mine iniquity in my bosom:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 31:33",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:31:33"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-034",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 34,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:31:34",
      "numberLabel": "34",
      "text": "Did I fear a great multitude, or did the contempt of families terrify me, that I kept silence, and went not out of the door?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 31:34",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:31:34"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-035",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 35,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:31:35",
      "numberLabel": "35",
      "text": "Oh that one would hear me! behold, my desire is, that the Almighty would answer me, and that mine adversary had written a book.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 31:35",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:31:35"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-036",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 36,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:31:36",
      "numberLabel": "36",
      "text": "Surely I would take it upon my shoulder, and bind it as a crown to me.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 31:36",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:31:36"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-037",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 37,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:31:37",
      "numberLabel": "37",
      "text": "I would declare unto him the number of my steps; as a prince would I go near unto him.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 31:37",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:31:37"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-038",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 38,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:31:38",
      "numberLabel": "38",
      "text": "If my land cry against me, or that the furrows likewise thereof complain;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 31:38",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:31:38"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-039",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 39,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:31:39",
      "numberLabel": "39",
      "text": "If I have eaten the fruits thereof without money, or have caused the owners thereof to lose their life:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 31:39",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:31:39"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-040",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 40,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:31:40",
      "numberLabel": "40",
      "text": "Let thistles grow instead of wheat, and cockle instead of barley. The words of Job are ended.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 31:40",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:31:40"
      }
    }
  ],
  "source": {
